# Newsletter campaign art, uploaded by an admin at send time and written into
# the web root by the compose screen. Runtime content, not source: committing
# it would put customer-facing campaign images in the repo, and every local
# test upload would show up as an untracked file.
#
# The URLs it serves ship inside emails that have already gone out, so this
# directory must SURVIVE deploys. That holds today because deploys are an
# in-place `git pull` (docs/OPERATIONS.md section 2). If the atomic-release
# work on the P1-3 roadmap lands, this has to become a shared directory
# symlinked into each release, as storage/ will have to be, or those URLs
# start 404ing.
/public/assets/newsletter/
/storage/partners.php

# Env backups — these contain REAL credentials and must never be committed.
.env.backup-*
.env.*.bak
.env.bak

# Local-only credential scratch notes. Real credentials belong in the
# password-manager vault (see docs/ONCALL.md escrow process), NEVER in git:
# repo history keeps them retrievable forever, even after deletion.
/docs/runbook/

# Personal planning / strategy notes — local only, never committed.
CTO.md
CTO_roadmap.md
crypto_implementation.md
crypto_gateway_decision.md
payment_provider_kill_switch_plan.md

# Local screenshot scratch and tool debug output, never source.
/scratch-pw/
/debug.log
# Laravel Boost writes a second copy of the project rules for tools that read
# the AGENTS.md convention instead of CLAUDE.md. Same content, different
# reader, and Boost rewrites it on every run. CLAUDE.md and .claude/skills are
# the committed source of truth, so the mirror stays local.
# rshop-audit is ours, not Boost's, and stays tracked.
/AGENTS.md
/.agents/skills/*
!/.agents/skills/rshop-audit/
